      "sentence_id": 1,
      "japanese": "これ何だ？－その３－「これ何だ？―その2―」で、古墳の大きさについて勉強しました。",
      "english_translation": "What is this? – \"What is this? – Part 2\" – We learned about the size of ancient tombs in that."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 2,
      "japanese": "日本で一番大きい古墳は何ですか？どれぐらいの長さですか？大きい古墳は、何県に多いですか？日本で一番大きな古墳は、前方後円墳の形をした大仙古墳です。",
      "english_translation": "What is the largest tomb in Japan? How long is it? Which prefecture has the most large tombs? The largest tomb in Japan is Ogonokōgakuin, a keyhole-shaped tumulus."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 3,
      "japanese": "大仙古墳は、大阪府にあります。",
      "english_translation": "The Oasayama Tumulus is located in Osaka Prefecture."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 4,
      "japanese": "そのような大きな前方後円墳は、奈良県や大阪府にたくさんあります。",
      "english_translation": "There are many large, linear tombs like this in Nara Prefecture and Osaka Prefecture."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 5,
      "japanese": "昔、奈良県のことを大和とよんでいました。",
      "english_translation": "In the past, Nara Prefecture was called Yamato."
    }
